<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (5\) Prioritise compound exercises:  These are exercises that use more than one muscle group/ joint at once. They have the most transferability to day to day activity as they train you to use your body as a unit. They should be the bread and butter of any exercise program. An example would be a push up, which uses the chest \(pectoralis major\), arms \(triceps\), shoulders \(anterior deltoids\) and other muscles which stabilise the body.  )
/E (5\) Prioritise compound exercises:  These are exercises that use more than one muscle group/ joint at once. They have the most transferability to day to day activity as they train you to use your body as a unit. They should be the bread and butter of any exercise program. An example would be a push up, which uses the chest \(pectoralis major\), arms \(triceps\), shoulders \(anterior deltoids\) and other muscles which stabilise the body.  )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
