<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Calorie deficit: This means that you consume less energy \(i.e. fewer calories\) than you expend. It is the underlying principle for every fat loss diet that exists, no matter how people spin it. Keto. Intermittent fasting. Low carb. None of these are magic. They are different methods of getting into a calorie deficit. Once in a calorie deficit, your body will look for other sources of energy such as fat, glycogen \(carbs stored in the muscles/liver\) or muscle tissue. Assuming your goal involves improving your body composition, you want to maximise fat loss  and minimise muscle loss.  Food quantity AND quality both matter. I will explain some principles for you to apply to help you make decisions with your food. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4 5]
>>
endobj
