>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (E.g.  75kg male office worker  Maintenance calories = 75 x 2.2 x  15 = 2475kcal \(10% = 248,  20% = 496\) Fat loss calories: 2475 - 248 = 2227kcal  \(10% deficit\) 2475 - 496 = 1979kcal \(20% deficit\) )
/E (E.g.  75kg male office worker  Maintenance calories = 75 x 2.2 x  15 = 2475kcal \(10% = 248,  20% = 496\) Fat loss calories: 2475 - 248 = 2227kcal  \(10% deficit\) 2475 - 496 = 1979kcal \(20% deficit\) )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Macronutrients explained: Macros are the source of all calories. These are protein, carbohydrates, and fats. The food we eat will be composed of different proportions of these 3 nutrients, and that will determine the amount of calories in the food. For reference, carbohydrates and protein both each have 4kcal per gram, and fat has 9kcal per gram \(alcohol has 7kcal per gram\).  For example, if 100g  kidney beans has 14g carbs \(14x4kcal\), 8g protein \(8x4kcal\), and 1g fat \(1x9kcal\) there would be around 97kcal total calories. You will notice a slight difference on nutrition label, but if you do the maths, the numbers will be close. )
/E (Macronutrients explained: Macros are the source of all calories. These are protein, carbohydrates, and fats. The food we eat will be composed of different proportions of these 3 nutrients, and that will determine the amount of calories in the food. For reference, carbohydrates and protein both each have 4kcal per gram, and fat has 9kcal per gram \(alcohol has 7kcal per gram\).  For example, if 100g  kidney beans has 14g carbs \(14x4kcal\), 8g protein \(8x4kcal\), and 1g fat \(1x9kcal\) there would be around 97kcal total calories. You will notice a slight difference on nutrition label, but if you do the maths, the numbers will be close. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
